    content: "# OpenTelemetry collector for selfhost. Agents send OTLP (gRPC on 4317, HTTP on 4318) with\n# `Authorization: Bearer <SELFHOST_OTLP_TOKEN>`. The collector batches, retries and forwards logs\n# and metrics to the selfhost API as OTLP/HTTP JSON. The API stores log records as ledger events.\n\nextensions:\n  health_check:\n    endpoint: 127.0.0.1:13133\n  bearertokenauth/agents:\n    scheme: Bearer\n    token: ${env:SELFHOST_OTLP_TOKEN}\n\nreceivers:\n  otlp:\n    protocols:\n      grpc:\n        endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4317\n        auth:\n          authenticator: bearertokenauth/agents\n      http:\n        endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4318\n        auth:\n          authenticator: bearertokenauth/agents\n\nprocessors:\n  memory_limiter:\n    check_interval: 1s\n    limit_percentage: 80\n    spike_limit_percentage: 20\n\nexporters:\n  otlp_http/selfhost:\n    # The exporter appends /v1/logs and /v1/metrics.\n    endpoint: http://selfhost:4400/v1/otlp\n    encoding: json\n    compression: gzip\n    headers:\n      Authorization: Bearer ${env:SELFHOST_TOKEN}\n    retry_on_failure:\n      enabled: true\n      max_elapsed_time: 10m\n    sending_queue:\n      enabled: true\n      batch:\n        flush_timeout: 1s\n        min_size: 1000\n        max_size: 1000\n  # Traces are not stored yet. They are accepted and dropped so agents with traces on do not log\n  # export errors.\n  nop:\n\nservice:\n  extensions: [health_check, bearertokenauth/agents]\n  pipelines:\n    logs:\n      receivers: [otlp]\n      processors: [memory_limiter]\n      exporters: [otlp_http/selfhost]\n    metrics:\n      receivers: [otlp]\n      processors: [memory_limiter]\n      exporters: [otlp_http/selfhost]\n    traces:\n      receivers: [otlp]\n      processors: [memory_limiter]\n      exporters: [nop]\n",
