    path: "Caddyfile",
    mode: 0o644,
    content: "# Caddy in front of selfhost (compose.tls.yml): HTTPS for SELFHOST_DOMAIN with a certificate it\n# gets and renews by itself, on ports 80 and 443. The selfhost API and the collector stay inside\n# Docker; this is the only way in.\n#\n#   /v1/*    the selfhost API, behind its bearer tokens (CLIs, hooks, the GitHub webhook)\n#   /otlp/*  agents' OpenTelemetry over HTTP, behind the agent token checked by the collector\n#   the rest the console, behind GitHub or Google sign-in when compose.signin.yml is in use\n\n# Without compose.signin.yml the console is closed: there is no sign-in to put in front of it.\n(console-closed) {\n\thandle {\n\t\trespond \"The selfhost console needs sign-in, which is not set up on this server. The API answers at /v1 with a bearer token.\" 503\n\t}\n}\n\n# With compose.signin.yml: oauth2-proxy checks the sign-in cookie on each request and sends\n# people without one to GitHub or Google first.\n(console-signin) {\n\thandle /oauth2/* {\n\t\treverse_proxy oauth2-proxy:4180\n\t}\n\thandle {\n\t\tforward_auth oauth2-proxy:4180 {\n\t\t\turi /oauth2/auth\n\t\t\t@signed_out status 401\n\t\t\thandle_response @signed_out {\n\t\t\t\tredir * /oauth2/sign_in?rd={scheme}://{host}{uri}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\troot * /srv/console\n\t\ttry_files {path} /index.html\n\t\tfile_server\n\t}\n}\n\n{$SELFHOST_DOMAIN} {\n\tencode zstd gzip\n\n\thandle /v1/* {\n\t\treverse_proxy selfhost:4400\n\t}\n\n\thandle_path /otlp/* {\n\t\treverse_proxy otel-collector:4318\n\t}\n\n\timport console-{$SELFHOST_CONSOLE_ACCESS:closed}\n}\n",
